# Target locations — EXAMPLE
# Copy this file to config/target_locations.txt and replace with your own places.
# Onboarding writes it from your geography answer.
#
# One place per line. Blank lines and # comments are ignored. Two uses:
#   1. The paid job-search feeds (RapidAPI) search these places.
#   2. Scoring: a posting whose US state or country is not listed scores 2
#      without an LLM call (Flag reason: location_mismatch). A posting the gate
#      cannot place (a city name alone, "See posting", blank) or a remote posting
#      in a listed country goes to the scorer, which caps an out-of-area role at 3.
#
# Forms: Remote / City, ST / City, Country (name in full) / United States
#   - A commute area that crosses a state line needs one line per state.
#   - Remote only: list Remote and your country.
#   - Open to the whole US: a single United States line.
#
# No file: the feeds search the whole United States and scoring has no gate.
# To turn the scoring gate off and keep the file, set FINDAJOB_LOCATION_GATE=off
# in data/.env.

Remote
United States
